Both integration tests pass — real parallel QuickJS with priming works.

Let me also do a quick end-to-end run of the actual binary with a small shard count to sanity-check the full pipeline (it should take ~20s serial equivalent; with SHARDS=4 on this machine let's see — the full suite locally per PR is ~6s at 8 workers on M-series; here let me try DMTOOLS_SUITE_SHARDS=4; the suite has 92 files and might take ~30-60s. Worth one run to verify exit codes and output.

Also — I want to empirically verify the top-level-throw priming inflation finding. I can craft a tiny reproduction: create a temp agents-like structure? That's complex. Simpler: reason from testRunner.js source — `action()` loop:

```js
for (var i = 0; i < testFiles.length; i++) {
    var filePath = testFiles[i];
    console.log('\n📂 ' + filePath);
    try {
        var testCode = file_read({ path: filePath });
        if (!testCode || !testCode.trim()) { ...continue; }
        eval(testCode);
    } catch (e) {
        _results_.failed++;
        console.log('  ❌ Error in test file: ' + ...);
    }
```

During priming, `test`/`suite` are stubs, but eval(testCode) of a prime file with a top-level `throw new Error('x')` (outside test/suite) → caught by action's catch → `_results_.failed++` on the REAL _results_ (not diverted). Each chunk priming that file adds +1 failed. The owning chunk adds +1 more (its own counted run of that file). Serial total: +1. So parallel totals ≠ serial totals: inflated by (number of chunks whose prime prefix contains the file). Confirmed by source reading. Also worth noting: the file's remaining top-level statements after the throw are skipped in EVERY chunk (and in serial too) — scope state parity for later files is maintained (they'd also see the truncated state in serial). OK.

Also note the docstring explicitly claims: "diverts result counting into a dump object" — not implemented. So it's a doc/code mismatch + latent totals inflation. IMPORTANT.

Let me run the actual binary end-to-end to verify exit code behavior. The agents/ submodule here — `git status` said "modified: agents (new commits)" — newer checkout, PR says 4 pre-existing failures with the newer agents (1270/4). So the run will exit 1 with failed=4 (if same as author's local). Let me run with DMTOOLS_SUITE_SHARDS=4 and observe. ~1-2 min. Let me do it.

